  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe strategy leverages a two-phase optimization: a global search using simulated annealing to escape local optima, followed by gradient-based refinement for precision. \n\n2. Mathematical specification\nDefine h as piecewise linear over [0,2], optimized to minimize max_k \u222bh(x)(1 - h(x+k))dx, subject to 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 and \u222bh=1.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n1. Initialize h with a triangular waveform or parent solution.\n2. Use simulated annealing for global exploration.\n3. Switch to gradient descent for refinement.\n4. Ensure constraints via projection.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nStart with initial_h_values if available; otherwise, use a triangular waveform. \nSimulated annealing parameters: initial temperature 0.1, cooling rate 0.95, 1000 iterations.\nGradient descent: learning rate 0.01, 5000 iterations.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nBudget 600s, with real-time checks. Save best solution every 60s.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nEnsure 0 \u2264 h \u2264 1 and \u222bh=1 within 1e-8 tolerance.",
